{
  "comment": "FabricDevice lists as the agent reports them in HostSettings (bytes received plus transmitted over window_seconds since its last report, from the sysfs port counters in 4-byte words) and whether the Controller raises network.rails-underused. Busy is at least 8 MiB/s, flat under 1% of the busy sibling, window at least 30 s. The Rust agent test reads every list through the generated contract and reads the sysfs sample as the agent_sample; the Controller test projects each case onto a node. Each case also gives the Spark's declared fabric_bandwidth_mbps (default 200000) and the network.fabric-* codes (default none) the Controller raises from the devices' rate_mbps and errors; network.fabric-down comes from telemetry and is tested there. A device without a window (the first report after a restart, a byte counter reset) gives only its port, active and rate_mbps. In agent_sample, expected_first is the first report and expected the second, and counters lists the six RDMA hw_counters then the netdev rx_errors and tx_errors, and rate is the port's rate file.",
